course: dictionary
lesson: 7606
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «Printing» is a good example, so read the whole sentence before you choose.
explain: «Before printing, books in Europe were copied by hand, so they were rare and very expensive.» Here printing means making books with a machine. The clues are books and copied by hand: people used to copy books by hand, and printing made copying much faster.
explain: «In 1517 Martin Luther criticised the Church, and printing spread his ideas quickly.» Printing here means making many copies of words on paper, so the ideas travelled fast. Check by swapping in your meaning: making copies of words fits, so you have chosen well.
fact: Printing means putting words or pictures on paper with a machine called a printer.
fact: Printing can also mean the job or business of making books and newspapers.
fact: Printing can mean writing with separate letters that are not joined, like printing your name in capital letters.
fact: In art, printing means pressing a shape with paint onto paper, like potato printing.
fact: The printing press made books cheap, so more people could learn to read.
exercise: «Before printing, books in Europe were copied by hand.» In this sentence, what does printing mean? | *Making books with a machine | Pressing paint onto leaves | Reading aloud to a class | Writing letters that are not joined
exercise: In art, the class makes pictures by pressing potatoes dipped in paint onto paper. What is the printing here? | Writing in joined-up writing | Copying books by hand | *Pressing a shape with paint onto paper | Putting words on paper with a printer
exercise: A printer prints 20 pages every minute. How many pages does it print in 5 minutes? | 15 pages | 25 pages | *100 pages | 4 pages
test: In handwriting, what does printing mean? | Drawing a picture with paint | Writing in joined-up writing | *Writing with separate letters that are not joined | Reading a book aloud
test: A printer makes 9 pages a minute. How many minutes will it take to print 45 pages? | 9 minutes | *5 minutes | 4 minutes | 36 minutes
exam: «In 1517 Martin Luther criticised the Church, and printing spread his ideas quickly.» What did printing do to his ideas? | Put them in a museum | Made them longer | *Spread them quickly | Made them disappear
